<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins Statoil pump contract.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins Statoil pump contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said on Thursday it had awarded Kvaerner Eureka, a division of Kvaerner ASA, a 100 million crown contract for the delivery of pump systems.</p>
<p>Due to run for five years, with options for another four years, the agreement also covers maintenance and service of pumps for future offshore developments, Statoil said.</p>
<p>The deal also includes a contract for pump maintenance on the Aasgard field off mid-Norway. This will run for five years and can be renewed for up to another 10 years.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
